Currently, Appsmith's canvas workspace allows developers to filter table widgets and collections using basic column match selections (e.g., filtering a table where Status == "Active"). It lacks a mechanism for app developers to build complex, multi-level boolean filter structures.
The Task: Implement a brand-new, user-facing "Query Filter Builder Widget" inside the Appsmith widget catalog layout ecosystem (app/client/src/widgets/). This layout component must give end-users an interactive editor to visually compose deeply nested boolean logical trees (handling AND / OR gates) along with variable input rows. For example, a user should be able to cleanly assemble an evaluation schema like: (AccountType == "Enterprise" AND Regions CONTAINS "US") OR (ARR > 50000).
